.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-roster-pin-tls - Pin a target's TLS key without touching its token


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge roster pin-tls <target-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Pin a target's API TLS key ([targets.tls] spki_sha256): the migration path
for a target bootstrapped before TLS pins existed. No token is read, written,
validated or sent.

.PP
For a target with SSH auth, the key pveproxy serves on the node itself is
captured over an SSH session pinned to the roster's stored host key, and the
target's address must serve the same key (source ssh-stored). For a target
without SSH auth, give the pin you verified by other means with --expect; the
address must serve exactly it (source expect). There is no trust-on-first-use
path. A CA-verified target (insecure_tls false) is pinned only explicitly,
with --expect: its chain is its identity, and a pin is the operator's choice.

.PP
A different stored pin is refused. --repin replaces it, for a target with SSH
auth only, whose pinned session vouches for the new key. --print captures and
checks, and writes nothing. The pin is written with a compare-and-set, under
the target's bootstrap lock.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--capture-port\fP=0
	pveproxy's port ON THE NODE, where the key is captured over SSH (default 8006)

.PP
\fB--expect\fP=""
	for a target without SSH auth: the pin you verified, sha256//<base64>; the target's address must serve exactly that key

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for pin-tls

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--print\fP[=false]
	capture and check the pin, and write nothing

.PP
\fB--repin\fP[=false]
	replace a different stored pin (a target with SSH auth only: its pinned session vouches for the new key)

.PP
\fB--ssh-port\fP=0
	SSH port on the target host (default: the port pveforge dials a target's stored SSH pin on, 22; the roster stores none)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-roster(1)\fP
